// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Root-cause synthesis across all three attempts:
//
// (A) SEMANTIC MISMATCH (37/49): Model opens << >> for the FIRST intermediate
//     sub-expression (e.g., <<n1*p1>>) and that becomes the last extracted span,
//     instead of the combined final formula <<n1*p1 + n2*p2 + n3*p3>>.
//     This is the dominant failure: the two-loop structure constrains whichever
//     << the model opens first, which is often a partial intermediate result.
//
// (B) "!!!!" DEAD-END FLOOD (attempt 3 only): Caused by the SINGLE-LOOP design
//     re-entering unconstrained mode after each span close. In unconstrained
//     mode the LM naturally generated long "!" chains. The two-loop structure
//     avoids this because Phase 2 exits only when EOS is returned (grammar
//     dead-ends mask all tokens except EOS) or budget is exhausted.
//
// (C) UNTERMINATED SPANS (3 examples): Budget exhaustion inside a dead-end
//     constrained span. Post-loop close guard "steps < maxSteps" prevents
//     closing when budget is exactly spent.
//
// Fix:
//   1. GUIDANCE: Strongly instruct the model NOT to use << >> for intermediate
//      steps. Write intermediate work in plain text and open << >> exactly once
//      for the COMPLETE combined final formula. Provide concrete counter-examples
//      showing the correct pattern vs. the wrong split pattern.
//   2. STRUCTURE: Two-loop design (best attempt). Grammatical dead-ends are
//      handled automatically: when only EOS is unmasked, AdaptiveConstrainedStep
//      returns eosToken and Phase 2 breaks cleanly—no "!!!!" flooding.
//   3. DEAD-END RECOVERY: Check DeadEndDetection after each constrained token.
//      On dead-end: RollbackConstrainedToComplete, then close. Ensures the span
//      is closed at the longest valid complete prefix rather than left open.
//   4. POST-LOOP CLOSE: Remove the `steps < maxSteps` gate; call
//      CloseConstrainedSpan whenever the span is complete at loop exit, even
//      if budget is fully spent (it adds one step beyond the loop, still
//      within maxSteps+1 … wait, must satisfy `cost <= maxSteps`). Guard with
//      `steps < maxSteps` but budget-reserve 1 step by stopping the Phase-2
//      loop at `steps < maxSteps - 1` when inside a span.
//   5. TOKEN-SKIP for early << >>: Count closed >> tokens. If fewer than 1
//      close has been seen and generated is short (<= 50 tokens), treat the
//      opening << as free text (do NOT enter constrained mode) so the model
//      can write its intermediate spans freely and we constrain only the
//      later final answer span.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END

// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// Invariant 1 (parser_validity):
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//
//   Phase 1 (unconstrained):
//     The implication is vacuously true while insideConstrainedOut = false.
//     Transition: we enter constrained mode only via the explicit assignment
//     `insideConstrainedOut := true; currentConstrainedOut := []`. The
//     precondition `parser.IsValidPrefix([])` holds by the method precondition,
//     so the invariant is re-established immediately.
//
//   Phase 2 (constrained):
//     Dead-end recovery path: RollbackConstrainedToComplete guarantees its
//     result rc is either IsCompletePrefix (which implies IsValidPrefix) or
//     empty (and IsValidPrefix([]) holds by precondition). We check
//     `IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut)` before calling
//     CloseConstrainedSpan, which exits constrained mode (implication becomes
//     vacuous). If not complete, we set insideConstrainedOut := false and
//     currentConstrainedOut := [] — vacuously true.
//     Normal path: AdaptiveConstrainedStep returns eosToken or a token t such
//     that IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut + [t]). On eosToken we break
//     without modifying span state. On t, AppendConstrainedToken postcondition
//     guarantees the updated currentConstrainedOut remains parser-valid.
//
//   Post-loop: CloseConstrainedSpan is guarded by `parser.IsCompletePrefix`
//   (checked explicitly) and exits constrained mode. Implication becomes vacuous.
//
// Invariant 2 (progress):
//   |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//
//   Phase 1: steps is incremented BEFORE any append. EOS appends nothing;
//   normal token appends exactly one; RenderedEndsWith check adds no tokens.
//   Bound preserved each iteration.
//
//   Phase 2 dead-end path: RollbackConstrainedToComplete may SHORTEN generated
